package hartland

model lexicon locale cs

// CN-P6 S6.1 T6 — the Czech words of the conceptual package (model/cn/*.ttrm), design `11` §1's forms. A concept's
// `label:` is no term; these are its words. A multi-word form is matched as written (the resolver's lemma lookup reads
// one-word mentions only — cs/automation.ttrm), so the cases a question uses are declared.
//
// What a concept term does (cn contracts §1.5): a span that matches it binds the CONCEPT, its landing as the binding's
// domain and the concept as `EntityBinding.concepts[]` (resolver ≥ 0.11.23). A phase phrase is longer than its
// bearer's word («pozastavené objednávky» against «objednávky»), so it wins the span (the longest covered span).
//
// No term repeats a word an element already carries, but «zákazník» (below): a word on an element lifts to the concepts
// grounded there (the archive's `liftsTo`), so «reklamace» reads `ReturnRequest`, «faktura» `Invoicing`, «tržby»
// `revenue` already, and a second term would only claim the word twice. «zákazník» is declared because S6.1 puts the
// bare word's DEFAULT sense on it: the role, never one of its phases.
//
// Held back, deliberately:
//   - the three channel phases (`StoreSale`, `WebSale`, `MarketplaceSale`): their words are the value labels of
//     `sales.channel` («tržiště», «web», «kanál prodejen»), which the Golem honours as a FILTER (md/hop HP-H). A phase
//     phrase would take the span from the label, and a Golem that reads no concept reading would lose the channel;
//   - `Return` ← «vratka»: the bare word is no term (lexicon/tests/store-family.test.mjs, until there is an all-channel
//     returns OBJECT to ask), and `channel_returns`, its landing, is not one yet (model/er/channel_returns.ttrm).
//
// `default: true` on «zákazník» only (S6.1 T6): a bare «zákazník» is the role, never a phase of it (AM-36).
//
// ⚑ For Bora's review — the Czech wording.

// ---- the role, and the revenue verb ----
def term customer_cn_cs {
    description: "zákazník — the customer role (the default sense of the bare word)"
    for: cn.Customer
    // The element's own word, deliberately (A-CN-8): cn.Customer grounds to er.entity.customer through the hop, so the
    // compiler suppresses the collision (RG-LEXC-004) and the resolver reads the pair as one sense (R-cn-1). This rule
    // has no cn view yet.
    // ttr-disable-next-line lexicon-form-collides-with-name
    forms: ["zákazník"]
    default: true
}
def term revenue_verb_cs {
    description: "utržit — what was taken in: the revenue quality (S6.2 T0's «utržili»)"
    for: cn.revenue
    forms: ["utržit", "utržili", "utržil", "utržila", "utržilo", "utržíme"]
}

// ---- orders (H-1) ----
def term pending_order_cs {
    description: "čekající objednávka — placed or held, waiting for its (re-)check"
    for: cn.PendingOrder
    forms: [
        "čekající objednávka", "čekající objednávky", "čekajících objednávek", "čekajícím objednávkám",
        "objednávka ke kontrole", "objednávky ke kontrole", "objednávek ke kontrole"
    ]
}
def term held_order_cs {
    description: "pozastavená objednávka — held"
    for: cn.HeldOrder
    forms: [
        "pozastavená objednávka", "pozastavené objednávky", "pozastavených objednávek", "pozastavenou objednávku",
        "blokovaná objednávka", "blokované objednávky", "blokovaných objednávek"
    ]
}
// Not «zadaná objednávka» (the phase's label): «objednávky zadané ve 3. čtvrtletí» are orders PLACED in a period, of
// any state (the corpus's d1), and a state phase would answer a different question.
def term placed_order_cs {
    description: "nezkontrolovaná objednávka — placed, not checked yet"
    for: cn.PlacedOrder
    forms: ["nezkontrolovaná objednávka", "nezkontrolované objednávky", "nezkontrolovaných objednávek"]
}
def term short_line_cs {
    description: "řádek bez krytí — a line its center cannot cover today"
    for: cn.ShortLine
    forms: [
        "řádek bez krytí", "řádky bez krytí", "řádků bez krytí", "řádku bez krytí",
        "nekrytý řádek", "nekryté řádky", "nekrytých řádků", "bez krytí"
    ]
}
def term mispriced_line_cs {
    description: "cenová odchylka — a line whose price is off the applicable one"
    for: cn.MispricedLine
    forms: [
        "cenová odchylka", "cenové odchylky", "cenových odchylek", "cenovou odchylkou", "cenovou odchylku",
        "řádek s odchylkou ceny", "řádky s odchylkou ceny", "řádků s odchylkou ceny"
    ]
}
def term overdue_invoice_cs {
    description: "faktura po splatnosti — open and past its due date"
    for: cn.OverdueInvoice
    forms: ["faktura po splatnosti", "faktury po splatnosti", "faktur po splatnosti", "fakturu po splatnosti", "fakturami po splatnosti"]
}
def term debtor_customer_cs {
    description: "zákazník po splatnosti, dlužník — a customer with an overdue invoice"
    for: cn.DebtorCustomer
    forms: [
        "zákazník po splatnosti", "zákazníci po splatnosti", "zákazníků po splatnosti", "zákazníky po splatnosti",
        "zákazníkům po splatnosti", "zákazník s fakturami po splatnosti", "zákazníci s fakturami po splatnosti",
        "zákazníků s fakturami po splatnosti", "dlužník", "dlužníci", "dlužníků", "dlužníky"
    ]
}

// ---- returns (H-2) ----
def term abusive_returner_cs {
    description: "zákazník s nadměrnými vratkami — whose return share is above the limit"
    for: cn.AbusiveReturner
    forms: [
        "nadměrné vratky", "nadměrných vratek", "zákazník s nadměrnými vratkami", "zákazníci s nadměrnými vratkami",
        "zákazníků s nadměrnými vratkami"
    ]
}
def term received_return_line_cs {
    description: "přijatý řádek reklamace — a return line waiting for its decision"
    for: cn.ReceivedReturnLine
    forms: ["přijatý řádek reklamace", "přijaté řádky reklamace", "přijatých řádků reklamace"]
}
def term bought_here_cs {
    description: "koupeno u nás — the returned item is on the order the request names"
    for: cn.BoughtHereLine
    forms: ["koupeno u nás", "koupené u nás", "zboží koupené u nás"]
}
def term late_return_line_cs {
    description: "reklamace po lhůtě — delivered longer ago than the return window"
    for: cn.LateReturnLine
    forms: ["reklamace po lhůtě", "řádek reklamace po lhůtě", "řádky reklamace po lhůtě", "řádků reklamace po lhůtě"]
}
def term small_value_line_cs {
    description: "řádek nízké hodnoty — a return line worth less than the small-value limit"
    for: cn.SmallValueLine
    forms: ["řádek nízké hodnoty", "řádky nízké hodnoty", "řádků nízké hodnoty"]
}
def term in_stock_at_center_cs {
    description: "skladem v centru zákazníka — the returned item is in stock at the customer's distribution center"
    for: cn.InStockAtCenter
    forms: ["skladem v centru zákazníka", "skladem v distribučním centru zákazníka"]
}
